 "t_flat_STATUS": "WITHDRAWN -- NOT INTERPRETABLE AT 100 Hz",
 "t_flat_WITHDRAWAL": {
  "status": "WITHDRAWN -- NOT INTERPRETABLE AT 100 Hz",
  "round": 307,
  "reason": "The .sto sampling interval is 0.010 s exactly (verified on disk: 1785 of 1785 intervals in R151S_s101, 1583 of 1583 in R291BF008_s152). t_flat is a time from heel strike to an early-stance minimum, so a SINGLE CYCLE's value can only land on a multiple of 0.010 s -- in this corpus 0.00/0.01/0.02/0.03/0.04. Every deposited cell figure is a mean of between 4 and 15 such quantised values, so the apparent resolution of the cell means is an artefact of averaging, not of measurement. The measured cell means span 0.012500 to 0.034667 s, i.e. the entire corpus lives inside roughly three sampling intervals. The smallest value demonstrates the quantisation outright: 0.012500 = (0.01 + 0.01 + 0.01 + 0.02) / 4 exactly, a four-cycle mean of a variable with three distinct levels.",
  "premise_corrections": "Two figures stated when this withdrawal was ordered did not match disk and are corrected here. (1) The value range is 0.012500-0.034667 s over all 66 cells, not 0.023-0.035 s; the narrower range covers only the C and S groups, while WPF reaches down to 0.012500. (2) The cell means are NOT uniformly 15-cycle means: n_cycles runs 4 to 15 across the 66 cells (observed values 4,5,6,8,9,10,11,12,13,15). Both corrections STRENGTHEN the withdrawal, because a 4-cycle mean of a three-level variable is coarser than a 15-cycle one.",
  "values_retained": "The values are deliberately NOT deleted. A withdrawn measurement stays readable so a later reader can see what was measured and why it was dropped; it simply stops being usable in any claim. t_flat appears in no live claim: it occurs zero times in RESULTS_3d_r214.md.",
  "measured_range_s": [
   0.0125,
   0.034667
  ],
  "sto_sampling_interval_s": 0.01,
  "n_cycles_range": [
   4,
   15
  ],
  "n_cells": 66,
  "withdrawal_was_ordered_earlier_but_never_written": "The withdrawal was decided in discussion and never became an artefact. For a reader holding only this directory it therefore did not exist. That gap is the defect this field closes, and it is the same failure the deposit rule exists to prevent."
 },
 "t_flat_f6_CONTROL_FLOOR": {
  "finding": "On the 6 Hz variant the control group is pinned at the quantisation floor: all 6 of 6 control cells read t_flat_f6 = 0.0 EXACTLY. Spastic cells read 0.000909-0.007500. W892 and W950 contain one exact zero each, and WPF contains five of 18.",
  "consequence": "No comparison against the control group on t_flat_f6 is meaningful, because that group has no variance and sits at the smallest representable value. A difference read off C vs S on this variant would be a floor effect, not a measurement.",
  "this_is_a_confirmation_not_an_anomaly": "SLAP_CUTOFF_SWEEP_r152.json found that a 6 Hz cutoff destroys this feature at zero noise on the OLD 2D corpus. This file's own why_both_filters note says that finding was re-measured here rather than carried over. The exact-zero control group IS that finding reproducing on the 3D corpus, and it reproduces in the direction r152 predicted.",
  "status": "Recorded r307. Previously visible in the deposited numbers but never stated."
 }
